    <string name="watchdog_title">MCU watchdog</string>
    <string name="watchdog_hint">At start and when waking from standby, the MCU waits for the SoC\'s \"ready\" (PC_READY): 10 s at most after standby, then it cuts the SoC. The service sends it again until the MCU answers, then the disarm frame (1F 05, PC_WDG_PAUSE).</string>
    <string name="watchdog_disarm">Disarm the watchdog at start</string>
    <string name="watchdog_disarm_hint">Sent after each PC_READY. Some firmwares ignore it (JCST 2024.08.09): PC_READY is what matters there</string>
    <string name="watchdog_toast">Notify at start</string>
    <string name="watchdog_from_file">Imposed by %1$s</string>
    <string name="watchdog_custom_frame">Frame from the config file: %1$s</string>
    <string name="watchdog_file_hint">Config file (optional, wins over these switches): /data/local/tmp/librehu-service.conf or Android/data/org.librehu.service/files/librehu-service.conf, lines watchdog.disarm=true|false, watchdog.toast=true|false, watchdog.frame=1F 05</string>
    <string name="watchdog_reload">Reload the file</string>
    <string name="mcu_reset_soc">Restart through the MCU</string>
    <string name="mcu_reset_soc_confirm">The MCU cuts the power of the SoC and turns it back on (MCU command 0E), like a hard reset: unsaved data is lost.</string>
